{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791101065,"nonce":"uX9XMQoG+Zbo4tw5KnkHXldYn90=","title":"Compile framework and library CSS to typed structs at compile time","message":"User direction (2026-10-04): the user-agent stylesheet (ashui.css.UserAgent.CSS) and library sheets (ashui.components' components.css, embedded by ashui.components.Sheet) are parsed at run time today, Stylesheet.parse on first use, a cost paid at start-up. Compile them instead: a macro runs CssParser over the source when the program is compiled and emits the Stylesheet as typed literals (rules, selectors, compounds, declarations, keyframes, variables, media), so run time only builds the index. Parse errors and unknown properties become compile errors at the CSS file's positions, as DeclaredCss already does for class names. Css.useUserAgent and Css.useLibrary take the compiled sheet; a page's own sheets loaded with Css.load or loadFile stay parsed at run time (live reload keeps working), and could opt into the same macro for sheets known at compile time.","files":null}]}